commit f779b5f1b31e78bb20a859de4b0ccf33dd807b10

C03: the subject the curiosity reader picks is grounded by the reader, like the news query (KNOWLEDGE1507)

KNOWLEDGE1505 measured that every topicless curiosity turn was decided as web.search with the chosen subject, but `_ground_explicit_arguments` requires the query to appear literally in the person's text and only the news query was exempt, so the eight turns asked back («¿Qué curiosidad me puedes contar?») with zero operations. When the request is a topicless curiosity and the query is one of the reader's subjects, the grounding now admits it with the schema validation intact; nothing else changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


